---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Chirag Singhal',
  url: 'https://oriz.in/about/',
  jobTitle: 'Software Engineer',
  description:
    'Software engineer specializing in scalable backend architectures, full-stack development, AI agents, and cloud-native deployments.',
  address: {
    '@type': 'PostalAddress',
    addressLocality: 'Bhubaneswar',
    addressRegion: 'Odisha',
    addressCountry: 'IN',
  },
  sameAs: [
    'https://github.com/chirag127',
    'https://x.com/chirag127',
    'https://linkedin.com/in/chirag127',
  ],
}
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Between"
  description="About Between, a relationships letter — practical, warm writing on communication, distance, and boundaries."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
 
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/">Between</a> / About</p>
    <h1>About</h1>
  </header>

  <article class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      Between is a relationships letter. Short, practical writing about the space
      two people share — how to talk in it, protect it, and keep it alive across
      distance.
    </p>

    <h2>What gets posted here</h2>
    <p>
      Letters you can use the same day: defusing a fight before it starts, saying
      the hard thing kindly, holding a boundary without guilt, keeping love
      steady when you live apart. No mysticism, no five-step cures — just clear
      moves that tend to help real people in real relationships.
    </p>

    <h2>The idea behind it</h2>
    <p>
      A relationship isn't one person or the other. It's the <em>between</em> —
      the thread that runs from you to them and back. That thread is the thing
      you can actually tend, and most of what helps is smaller and plainer than
      we expect. That's what this letter is for.
    </p>

    <h2>Who writes it</h2>
    <p>
      I'm Chirag Singhal. I write Between as part of the
      <a href="https://oriz.in">oriz</a> family of sites — useful, free, and
      quiet. No newsletters you didn't ask for, no popups, no paid tier.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email: <a href="mailto:whyiswhen@gmail.com">whyiswhen@gmail.com</a>.
      Or use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head { padding-block: 3rem 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); max-width: var(--container-prose, 720px); margin-inline: auto; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--color-fg-muted); font-size: 0.8125rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .eyebrow a { color: var(--color-fg-muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .eyebrow a:hover { color: var(--color-fg); }
  h1 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0; }
  .prose { padding-block: 2.5rem 4rem; color: var(--color-prose); line-height: 1.75; font-size: 1.0625rem; max-width: var(--container-prose, 720px); margin-inline: auto; }
  .prose .lede { font-size: 1.1875rem; color: var(--color-fg); margin: 0 0 2rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-fg); margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  .prose a { color: var(--color-accent); }
</style>
